# Cross-Platform Enforcement

**Trigger**: Apply when writing, editing, or reviewing any rule or skill file that contains shell commands.

## Core Requirement

All shell commands in rules and skills MUST be cross-platform compatible:

1. **Use cross-platform tools** (pnpm, git, docker, rg) when possible
2. **Provide PowerShell equivalents** alongside Unix-style commands
3. **Replace `bash` code blocks with `powershell`** unless Docker/CI-only
4. **Link to powershell-commands-windows.mdc** for Windows reference

## Shell Command Checklist

Before publishing any rule or skill, check:

- [ ] No `bash` code blocks without PowerShell equivalent
- [ ] No `cd &&` chains without PowerShell 7+ note or alternative
- [ ] No `#!/bin/bash` scripts without cross-platform alternative
- [ ] Path separators documented (`\` for Windows native, `/` for Docker/git)
- [ ] References `powershell-commands-windows.mdc` if shell-heavy

## OS Command Reference Table

When writing shell commands, check this mapping:

| Unix Command | Windows/PowerShell Equivalent | Cross-Platform Alternative |
|---|---|---|
| `ls` | `Get-ChildItem` | — |
| `cat` | `Get-Content` | — |
| `grep` | `Select-String` | `rg` (ripgrep) |
| `find` | `Get-ChildItem -Recurse` | `fd` |
| `rm` | `Remove-Item` | — |
| `mkdir` | `New-Item -ItemType Directory` | — |
| `cd dir && cmd` | `Set-Location dir; cmd` | Separate commands |
| `export VAR=val` | `$env:VAR = "val"` | — |
| `curl URL` | `Invoke-WebRequest -Uri URL` | — |
| `chmod +x` | Not needed (use `.ps1` extension) | — |

## Code Block Format

**Preferred format** — single PowerShell block (cross-platform tools):

```powershell
pnpm run build
pnpm run test
```

**Alternative format** — both Unix and Windows (when native commands differ):

```powershell
# Windows / PowerShell
Set-Location src
pnpm run test
```

```bash
# Unix / bash (CI or Docker)
cd src
pnpm run test
```

## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `bash` block without PowerShell equivalent | Fails on Windows | Add `powershell` block or use cross-platform tool |
| `cd backend && pytest` | PowerShell 5.1 lacks `&&` | Use separate commands: `Set-Location backend; pytest` |
| `#!/bin/bash` entrypoint | Windows lacks bash | Use PowerShell script or Node.js script |
| Unix paths `src/components` in PowerShell | May fail in some contexts | Use `src\components` or `Join-Path` |

## Enforcement

When reviewing a rule or skill:

1. Grep for `bash` code blocks — flag if no PowerShell equivalent
2. Grep for `cd &&` patterns — flag if no PowerShell 7+ note
3. Grep for `#!/bin/bash` — flag if no Windows alternative
4. Verify shell-heavy files reference `powershell-commands-windows.mdc`

